Z||000000||x cuda man||01-03-2000||12:40 PM||||i've got a (86se auto)that i bought from a friend,this car has been parked for 2 years and needs fixing up, but its not that bad.i also have 2 cars setting in the back yard that i need to get rid of(81 maxxima and 86 rs cavalier)i am going to trash'em.i never got the title for the maxxima and cavalier's got a bad engine.(4 banger auto)i was just thinking,the fiero was built from the gm parts bin,should i keep the cavalier for parts or let it go? are there any parts that interchange? thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||01-03-2000||08:34 PM||||The cav tranny should work in any fiero auto. will need the linkage on the tranny changed I think. Most of the rest of the motor, what ever is left that's good, will also work.<P>Some interior parts will work. steering column for one should work. Can't really say for sure what else. I think the wheels should fit. If you have the plastic lug caps on the fiero(used with AL wheels mainly) save them from the cav if it's got 'em too. Those stupid things are about 2$ each to replace.||||reg||1
